{# roomhive/host/base.html.twig
   SHARED HOST SHELL — shared site navbar + collapsible host sidebar.
   Every host page extends this and only provides a content block.

   The sidebar is a 1:1 port of legacy host/host_sidebar.php:
     - 9 main links + 5 Settings links + 1 footer link + Log Out
     - Collapsible (250px → 66px), chevron toggle, localStorage key
       'roomhive_host_sidebar_collapsed' (own key, separate from the
       user sidebar's)
     - Red badge pills: Pending Tenants (pending_tenants_count) +
       Notifications (notification_count); collapsed state shows a
       small dot pinned to the icon's top-right
     - "Quit Hosting" in red; collapsed links get title tooltips

   === VISUAL FIX (this version — verified against the legacy
   screenshot with a pixel-matched side-by-side render) ===
     - ACTIVE link now carries the amber LEFT ACCENT BAR:
       inset 5px box-shadow in --rh-accent, following the pill's
       rounded corners (the legacy "Overview" pill shows a solid
       amber bar on its left edge — sampled #e1a83d off the shot).
     - INACTIVE link color darkened var(--rh-muted) → #3f4750:
       the legacy labels + icons sample at near-ink slate
       (#454a4f stroke cores), noticeably darker than muted gray.
     - SETTINGS heading gray nudged #9aa5b1 → #949ba6.
     Everything else (pill bg, badge red, Poppins, rhythm, icons)
     already sampled identical.

   === SIDEBAR FREEZE + OWN SCROLLBAR (this version) ===
     - The rail no longer scrolls away with the page: on desktop
       it is position:fixed, pinned 90px below the top edge at the
       left edge of the centered 1280px container — scrolling the
       main content leaves it frozen in place.
     - (Why not sticky: sticky only freezes while no ancestor is a
       scroll container — a single overflow rule on <body> in the
       global stylesheet silently disables it for every descendant,
       and this template doesn't control the global CSS. fixed
       carries no such dependency.)
     - The rail is capped to the space under the navbar
       (max-height: calc(100vh - 110px)): when the 15 links +
       Settings group + Log Out don't fit the screen, it scrolls
       INSIDE itself with its own slim theme-aware scrollbar
       instead of being cut off at the fold.
     - fixed takes the rail out of the flex flow, so the content
       column re-aligns itself with margin-left (250px rail +
       22px gap = 272px, transitioned 0.3s to match the rail's
       width animation). The collapse toggle now also flips a
       body.rh-side-collapsed class (one added line in the JS) and
       the column shifts back to 66px + 22px = 88px in sync — the
       collapse reflow still closes the gap like before.
     - Below 900px everything reverts to the old stacked layout:
       static full-width rail, no cap, no internal scroll, no
       column offset.

   ACTIVE-NAV KEYS (set in the child template):
     overview | listings | pending | bookings | earnings | payouts |
     reviews | messages | notifications | editprofile | verification |
     payoutmethods | notificationsettings | security | quithosting |
     helpcenter
     ('verification' has no sidebar link — a host verification page
     can set active_nav='verification' and nothing highlights, same
     as the legacy behavior)

   LEGACY → SYMFONY URL MAP (unported pages are TODO routes — the
   links will 404 until those legacy files are pasted and ported):
     overview            → /host/profile              ✓ ported
     listings            → /host/listings             (mylistings.php)
     pending             → /host/pending-tenants      (pendingtenants.php)
     bookings            → /host/bookings             (hostbookings.php)
     earnings            → /host/earnings             (hostearnings.php)
     payouts             → /host/payouts              (payouts.php)
     reviews             → /host/reviews              (hostreviews.php)
     messages            → /host/messages             (hostmessages.php)
     notifications       → /host/notifications        (hostnotifications.php)
     editprofile         → /host/profile/edit         (hosteditprofile.php)
     payoutmethods       → /host/payout-methods       (payoutmethods.php)
     notificationsettings→ /host/notification-settings(hostnotificationsettings.php)
     security            → /host/security             (hostsecurity.php)
     quithosting         → /host/quit-hosting         (quithosting.php)
     helpcenter          → /host/help                 (helpcenter.php)

   === TOPBAR → SHARED NAVBAR (this version) ===
   The placeholder topbar (logo, bell, theme toggle, host chip
   dropdown) is removed. The real shared navbar — the Twig port of
   legacy includes/navbar.php — is now included at the top of every
   host page, so hosts see the same header as user pages: logo,
   menu links, bell with unread badge, and the MY PROFILE dropdown
   (whose first entry reads "Host Dashboard" → /host/profile for
   hosts). The host's avatar photo is forwarded to the navbar via
   nav_avatar. The old chip-menu Security link that still pointed
   at /settings is gone with the placeholder.

   Dark mode: still applied on load from localStorage 'rhTheme'
   (body[data-theme="dark"]); the toggle itself lives on the
   settings page, same as the legacy layout.

   Lucide: loaded once by the navbar's guarded loader — this shell
   no longer ships its own copy (same __rhNavbarLucide guard key).

   Controller contract — each host page passes:
     host (name/avatar/email), notification_count,
     pending_tenants_count
#}
{% import 'admin/_macros.html.twig' as ui %}

{# ---- Sidebar link groups (key, url, icon, label) ---- #}
{% set side_badges = {
    'pending':       pending_tenants_count|default(0),
    'notifications': notification_count|default(0),
} %}

{% set side_main = [
    {key: 'overview',      href: '/host/profile',            icon: 'layout-dashboard', label: 'Overview'},
    {key: 'listings',      href: '/host/listings',           icon: 'building-2',       label: 'My Listings'},
    {key: 'pending',       href: '/host/pending-tenants',    icon: 'user-plus',        label: 'Pending Tenants'},
    {key: 'bookings',      href: '/host/bookings',           icon: 'calendar-check',   label: 'Bookings'},
    {key: 'earnings',      href: '/host/earnings',           icon: 'banknote',         label: 'Earnings'},
    {key: 'payouts',       href: '/host/payouts',            icon: 'hand-coins',       label: 'Payouts'},
    {key: 'reviews',       href: '/host/reviews',            icon: 'star',             label: 'Reviews'},
    {key: 'messages',      href: '/host/messages',           icon: 'message-square',   label: 'Messages'},
    {key: 'notifications', href: '/host/notifications',      icon: 'bell',             label: 'Notifications'},
] %}
{% set side_settings = [
    {key: 'editprofile',          href: '/host/profile/edit',        icon: 'user-round',   label: 'Profile & Account'},
    {key: 'notificationsettings', href: '/host/notification-settings', icon: 'bell-ring', label: 'Notification Settings'},
    {key: 'security',             href: '/host/security',            icon: 'shield',       label: 'Security'},
    {key: 'quithosting',          href: '/host/quit-hosting',        icon: 'door-open',    label: 'Quit Hosting'},
] %}
{% set side_footer = [
    {key: 'helpcenter', href: '/host/help', icon: 'circle-help', label: 'Help Center'},
] %}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <title>{% block page_title %}Host — RoomHive{% endblock %}</title>
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

        {# Anti-flash dark-mode bootstrap (matches legacy rhTheme convention) #}
        <script>
            try {
                if (localStorage.getItem("rhTheme") === "dark") {
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme-preview", "1");
                }
            } catch (e) {}
        </script>

        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
        <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('assets/style.css') }}">
        <script>
            document.documentElement.classList.add("js");
        </script>

        <style>
            :root {
                --rh-ink: #1c2a38;
                --rh-muted: #66788a;
                --rh-line: #e6ebf1;
                --rh-card: #ffffff;
                --rh-accent: #eda423;
                --rh-accent-light: #fff4e0;
                --rh-radius: 16px;
            }
            * {
                box-sizing: border-box;
            }
            body {
                font-family: "Poppins", sans-serif;
                background: #f6f7fb;
                color: var(--rh-ink);
                margin: 0;
                min-height: 100vh;
            }

            /* ===== Layout ===== */
            .host-layout {
                display: flex;
                align-items: flex-start;
                max-width: 1280px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                padding: 90px 20px 40px;
                gap: 22px;
            }
            .host-content {
                flex: 1 1 auto;
                min-width: 0;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 20px;
                /* the fixed rail no longer occupies flex space, so the
                                                       column offsets itself: 250px rail + 22px gap;
                                                       transitioned so it closes up in sync when the rail
                                                       collapses (66px + 22px below) */
                margin-left: 272px;
                transition: margin-left 0.3s ease;
            }
            body.rh-side-collapsed .host-content {
                margin-left: 88px;
            }

            /* =========================================================
                                                                                       COLLAPSIBLE HOST SIDEBAR — 1:1 port of host_sidebar.php.
                                                                                       Profile card removed (this version) — links start flush
                                                                                       at the top, matching the user sidebar.
                                                                                    ========================================================= */
            .hp-sidebar {
                /* ---- spacing knobs ---- */
                --hp-w: 250px;
                --hp-w-collapsed: 66px;
                --hp-icon: 18px;
                --hp-gap: 10px;
                --hp-link-pad-y: 10px;
                --hp-link-pad-x: 14px;

                /* frozen rail: pinned under the navbar at the left
                                                       edge of the centered 1280px container — scrolling
                                                       the main content no longer moves it */
                position: fixed;
                top: 90px;
                left: max(20px, calc(50% - 620px));
                flex-shrink: 0;

                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 3px;

                width: var(--hp-w);
                box-sizing: border-box;
                background: #fff;
                border: 1px solid var(--rh-line);
                border-radius: var(--rh-radius);
                padding: 12px 10px;

                transition: width 0.3s ease;

                /* ---- its own scrollbar ----
                                                       capped to the space under the navbar: when the
                                                       links don't fit the screen, the rail scrolls
                                                       inside itself instead of being cut off */
                max-height: calc(100vh - 110px);
                overflow-y: auto;
                overflow-x: hidden;
                scrollbar-width: thin;
                scrollbar-color: #cdd6e0 transparent;
            }

            /* ---- the rail's own scrollbar (light theme) ---- */
            .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar {
                width: 6px;
            }
            .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
                background: transparent;
            }
            .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
                background: #cdd6e0;
                border-radius: 999px;
            }
            .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
                background: #b7c2cf;
            }

            /* ---- chevron toggle ---- */
            .hp-side-toggle {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                width: 100%;
                padding: 6px 4px;
                margin: 0 0 4px;
                background: transparent;
                border: none;
                border-radius: 8px;
                color: inherit;
                font: inherit;
                cursor: pointer;
                transition: background 0.2s ease;
            }
            .hp-side-toggle:hover {
                background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
            }
            .hp-side-toggle .icon {
                width: 20px;
                height: 20px;
                transition: transform 0.3s ease;
            }

            /* ---- links ---- */
            .hp-side-link {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: var(--hp-gap);
                padding: var(--hp-link-pad-y) var(--hp-link-pad-x);
                margin: 0;
                white-space: nowrap;
                position: relative;
                font-size: 13px;
                font-weight: 600;
                color: #3f4750; /* legacy: near-ink slate, darker than --rh-muted */
                text-decoration: none;
                border-radius: 10px;
                transition:
                    background 0.2s ease,
                    color 0.2s ease;
            }
            .hp-side-link:hover {
                background: #f6f7fb;
                color: var(--rh-ink);
            }
            .hp-side-link.active {
                background: var(--rh-accent-light);
                color: #b07708;
                /* amber left accent bar — follows the rounded corners */
                box-shadow: inset 5px 0 0 var(--rh-accent);
            }
            .hp-side-link .icon {
                width: var(--hp-icon);
                height: var(--hp-icon);
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }
            .hp-side-label {
                min-width: 0;
                overflow: hidden;
                text-overflow: ellipsis;
            }

            /* ---- badges ---- */
            .hp-side-badge {
                margin-left: auto;
                background: #e14b4b;
                color: #fff;
                font-size: 11px;
                font-weight: 700;
                line-height: 1;
                padding: 3px 7px;
                border-radius: 999px;
            }

            /* ---- Settings group heading ---- */
            .hp-side-heading {
                margin: 14px 10px 4px;
                font-size: 11px;
                font-weight: 800;
                letter-spacing: 1px;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                color: #949ba6;
            }

            .hp-side-quit {
                color: #b3261e;
            }
            .hp-side-quit:hover {
                background: #fdecea;
                color: #b3261e;
            }

            /* =========================================================
                                                                                       COLLAPSED STATE
                                                                                    ========================================================= */
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed {
                width: var(--hp-w-collapsed);
            }
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-toggle {
                justify-content: center;
            }
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-toggle .icon {
                transform: rotate(180deg);
            }
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-label,
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-heading {
                display: none;
            }
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-link {
                justify-content: center;
                gap: 0;
                padding-left: 0;
                padding-right: 0;
            }
            /* badge becomes a small dot pinned to the icon's top-right */
            .hp-sidebar.collapsed .hp-side-badge {
                position: absolute;
                top: 4px;
                left: calc(50% + 2px);
                margin-left: 0;
                min-width: 15px;
                height: 15px;
                padding: 0 4px;
                font-size: 9px;
                line-height: 15px;
                text-align: center;
            }

            .hp-side-logout {
                margin-top: 10px;
            }

            /* ---- Card base (shared by host pages) ---- */
            .hp-card {
                background: #fff;
                border: 1px solid var(--rh-line);
                border-radius: var(--rh-radius);
                padding: 22px;
            }
            .hp-card-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 12px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
            }
            .hp-card-header h3 {
                margin: 0;
                font-size: 16px;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rh-ink);
            }
            .hp-muted {
                font-size: 12px;
                color: var(--rh-muted);
            }
            .hp-btn-outline {
                display: inline-block;
                padding: 8px 16px;
                border-radius: 9px;
                border: 1px solid var(--rh-accent);
                color: var(--rh-accent);
                background: #fff;
                font-size: 12px;
                font-weight: 700;
                text-decoration: none;
                transition: background 0.15s ease;
            }
            .hp-btn-outline:hover {
                background: var(--rh-accent-light);
            }

            @media (max-width: 900px) {
                /* stacked layout again: normal-flow full-width rail,
                                                       no cap / internal scroll, no column offset */
                .hp-sidebar {
                    position: static;
                    left: auto;
                    max-height: none;
                    width: 100%;
                }
                body.rh-side-collapsed .host-content,
                .host-content {
                    margin-left: 0;
                }
                .host-layout {
                    flex-direction: column;
                    padding: 90px 16px 40px;
                }
            }

            /* ---- Dark mode ---- */
            body[data-theme="dark"] {
                background: #0d1218;
                color: #e8ecf1;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-toggle:hover {
                background: #1a222b;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-sidebar {
                background: #141b24;
                border-color: #1a222b;
                scrollbar-color: #2c3742 transparent;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
                background: #2c3742;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
                background: #3a4653;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-link {
                color: #8d99a5;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-link:hover {
                background: #1a222b;
                color: #e8ecf1;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-link.active {
                background: rgba(237, 164, 35, 0.15);
                color: #f6c04e;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-heading {
                color: #6b7684;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-quit {
                color: #f28b82;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-side-quit:hover {
                background: rgba(226, 74, 61, 0.15);
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-card {
                background: #141b24;
                border-color: #1a222b;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-card-header h3 {
                color: #e8ecf1;
            }
            body[data-theme="dark"] .hp-muted {
                color: #8d99a5;
            }

            @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
                .hp-sidebar,
                .host-content,
                .hp-side-toggle .icon,
                .hp-side-link {
                    transition: none;
                }
            }
        </style>
        {% block styles %}{% endblock %}
    </head>
    <body>

        {# ============ SHARED SITE NAVBAR (port of includes/navbar.php) ============
           Same header as user pages: logo, menu, bell + unread badge,
           MY PROFILE dropdown (first entry reads "Host Dashboard" for
           hosts → /host/profile). The host's avatar photo is forwarded
           so the navbar shows the real photo instead of the fallback
           icon. #}
        {% set nav_avatar = host.avatar|default('') %}
        {% include 'partials/navbar.html.twig' %}

        <div class="host-layout">

            {# ============ COLLAPSIBLE HOST SIDEBAR ============ #}
            <aside class="hp-sidebar" id="hpSidebar">

                {# Expand / Collapse toggle #}
                <button type="button" class="hp-side-toggle" id="hpSidebarToggle" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Collapse sidebar">
                    {{ ui.icon('chevron-left') }}
                </button>

                {# Main links — start flush at the top, user-sidebar style #}
                {% for item in side_main %}
                    <a
                        href="{{ item.href }}"
                        class="hp-side-link{{ active_nav|default('') == item.key ? ' active' : '' }}"
                    >
                        {{ ui.icon(item.icon) }}
                        <span class="hp-side-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
                        {% if (side_badges[item.key] ?? 0) > 0 %}
                            <span class="hp-side-badge">{{ side_badges[item.key] }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}

                {# Settings group #}
                <span class="hp-side-heading">Settings</span>
                {% for item in side_settings %}
                    <a
                        href="{{ item.href }}"
                        class="hp-side-link{{ (item.key == 'quithosting' ? ' hp-side-quit' : '') }}{{ active_nav|default('') == item.key ? ' active' : '' }}"
                    >
                        {{ ui.icon(item.icon) }}
                        <span class="hp-side-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
                        {% if (side_badges[item.key] ?? 0) > 0 %}
                            <span class="hp-side-badge">{{ side_badges[item.key] }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}

                {# Footer #}
                {% for item in side_footer %}
                    <a
                        href="{{ item.href }}"
                        class="hp-side-link{{ active_nav|default('') == item.key ? ' active' : '' }}"
                    >
                        {{ ui.icon(item.icon) }}
                        <span class="hp-side-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
                        {% if (side_badges[item.key] ?? 0) > 0 %}
                            <span class="hp-side-badge">{{ side_badges[item.key] }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}

                <a href="/logout" class="hp-side-link hp-side-logout">
                    {{ ui.icon('logout') }}
                    <span class="hp-side-label">Log Out</span>
                </a>

            </aside>

            {# ============ CONTENT COLUMN ============ #}
            <div class="host-content">
                {% block content %}{% endblock %}
            </div>
        </div>

        <script>
            /* =====================================================
                                                                                       SHARED HOST UI SCRIPT — dark mode apply + SIDEBAR
                                                                                       COLLAPSE (own localStorage key, separate from the
                                                                                       user sidebar's; the toggle also mirrors its state
                                                                                       onto <body> as rh-side-collapsed so the fixed
                                                                                       rail's content column re-aligns in CSS).
                                                                                       The chip dropdown and theme-toggle click handler
                                                                                       were removed with the placeholder topbar: the
                                                                                       navbar has its own dropdown, and the theme toggle
                                                                                       lives on the settings page (legacy).
                                                                                    ====================================================== */
            (function () {
                "use strict";

                /* ---- Dark mode: apply saved theme on load ---- */
                try {
                    if (localStorage.getItem("rhTheme") === "dark") {
                        document.body.setAttribute("data-theme", "dark");
                        document.documentElement.removeAttribute("data-theme-preview");
                    }
                } catch (e) {}

                /* ---- Sidebar collapse (ported from host_sidebar.php) ----
                                                                                           Same behavior as the user sidebar but with its OWN
                                                                                           localStorage key. */
                var sidebar = document.getElementById("hpSidebar");
                var sideToggle = document.getElementById("hpSidebarToggle");
                if (sidebar && sideToggle) {
                    var STORAGE_KEY = "roomhive_host_sidebar_collapsed";
                    var links = sidebar.querySelectorAll(".hp-side-link");

                    function updateTitles(collapsed) {
                        links.forEach(function (link) {
                            var label = link.querySelector(".hp-side-label");
                            if (collapsed) {
                                link.setAttribute("title", label ? label.textContent : "");
                            } else {
                                link.removeAttribute("title");
                            }
                        });
                    }

                    function applyState(collapsed) {
                        sidebar.classList.toggle("collapsed", collapsed);
                        /* mirror onto <body> so the content column
                                                               shifts back in sync while the rail narrows */
                        document.body.classList.toggle("rh-side-collapsed", collapsed);
                        sideToggle.setAttribute(
                            "aria-expanded",
                            collapsed ? "false" : "true",
                        );
                        sideToggle.setAttribute(
                            "aria-label",
                            collapsed ? "Expand sidebar" : "Collapse sidebar",
                        );
                        updateTitles(collapsed);
                    }

                    var savedCollapsed = false;
                    try {
                        savedCollapsed = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY) === "1";
                    } catch (e) {}
                    applyState(savedCollapsed);

                    sideToggle.addEventListener("click", function () {
                        var nowCollapsed = !sidebar.classList.contains("collapsed");
                        applyState(nowCollapsed);
                        try {
                            localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, nowCollapsed ? "1" : "0");
                        } catch (e) {}
                    });
                }
            })();
        </script>
        {% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
        {# Lucide is loaded once by the navbar's guarded loader
           (window.__rhNavbarLucide) — no second copy here. #}
    </body>
</html>
